===============QTI SEPOLICY =================================. 
All vendor related sepolicy (cil) files are going to be added here .

During the pre-phase of build all this files are copied to upstream 
code in the below path . 
build_dir/target-arm_cortex-a7+neon-vfpv4_musl_eabi/selinux-policy-0.8

Any contribution to this folder please follow the folder tree and naming 
convention of upstream  you can refer to the above path  under /src 
you can see different cil file   place in each directory based on the type of 
resource /bin.


Folder Org :

├── cil
│   ├── dev
│   │   └── nodedev
│   ├── file
│   │   └── execfile
│   │       └──test
│   ├── initscript
│   └── upstream
├── files

1st Level :  cil:  contails all the sepolicy files
             files : place holder for patches to selinux upstream code
2nd level :
            dev -> place holder for all device nodes /dev....
            nodedev -> mostly device node added
            files:  conteails all the  execfiles/binfile/libs sepolicy
            initscript : hold as the initscript related seploicy
            upstream :   this will hold all the  sepolicy needed for upstream service
            test folder : use this folder for policy writen for test code .

Make file:
Local reference of Makefile:
package/system/selinux-policy/Makefile
https://git.openwrt.org/?p=openwrt/openwrt.git;a=blob;f=package/system/selinux-policy/Makefile

To compile just sepolicy :
 make -j16  V=sc  package/system/selinux-policy

 Please note: Qti sepolicy change will only take effect once you clean and  rebuild SEpolicy
 to clean and compile just sepolicy
  make -j16  V=sc  package/system/selinux-policy/clean
  make -j16  V=sc  package/system/selinux-policy/compile
 Once done  create the full build

 As we are enabling  global selinux to enforce  we have to take care of upstream sepolicy
 All uptream sepolicy  are added to  qexec and qlibs  cil file

#### Policy restriction
#1. dac_override/dac_search  are allowed for upstream only  - TOBE FIXED
#2. exemem and exemod   are allowed only for upstream      native code should still use PIC /PIE flag


For example you can refer
build_dir/target-arm_cortex-a7+neon-vfpv4_musl_eabi/selinux-policy-0.8/src

22.0.3 version update
with future upgrade to 22.0.3 selinux version will change from 0.8 to 1.1

Other doc/links :
https://openwrt.org/packages/pkgdata/selinux-policy

####user_debug variable

for DEBUG varaint we exposed user_debugas a global variable which can be used across  all the cil files (upstream and downstream)

user_dedug will set to 0 if variant is selected as USER

#declaration
<workspace_location>/owrt-qti-sepolicy/cil/files/execute/user_debug/userdebug.cil

# user_debug 

user_debug is a global boolean varaible exposed by downstream selinux cil file <userdebug.cil> for DEBUG variant

## How to use user_debug with cil file
## Gnerally the case will be like you have rule in debug build but not on production build . So add rule if debug build and noting in user build.

    (booleanif user_debug
        (true
            (allow subj xyz.conffile (file (rw_file_perms)))
        )
    )


